    {
      "marker": "7",
      "text": "7. The major consists of at least 35-36 hours taken at the 300-level or above of USC coursework and 15 of those credit hours must be at the 400-level or above (including HRSM 497). The major coursework includes 30 hours of courses organized in one of two approaches and this is determined by the student with the advisor’s approval. a. Specializations have at least 15 hours in each of two areas. Each course proposed must correspond to the intent of the Specialization. i. One area must be from one department within the College of HRSM and include a minimum of at least 15 credit hours. ii. The other area is determined by the student with the advisor’s approval and must include a minimum of at least 15 credit hours. b. Thematic model has at least 10 courses that correspond directly to a theme and that, when viewed collectively, will establish a minimum amount of depth in a chosen theme. The thematic approach must result in at least 30 credit hours. i. The thematic model must include at least 15 credit hours taken within the courses offered by the College of HRSM.",
